<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Innu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Montagnais</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Innu, called Montagnais by the French, are an Indigenous people of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/labrador">Labrador</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> who traditionally lived by hunting caribou and fishing. Their alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain">Samuel de Champlain</a> against the Iroquois, made at Tadoussac in 1603, helped found the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> on the St Lawrence. Their language belongs to the Algonquian family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/innu.jpg" alt="Innu" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Davis_Inlet_1903.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
